---
import editorShot from "../assets/screens/editor.webp";
import paletteShot from "../assets/screens/palette.webp";
import permissionsShot from "../assets/screens/permissions.webp";
---

<section class="section section--roomy interface" id="interface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Two panes, no surprises.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The patterns of your file manager, with the protocol’s state on screen.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="shot shot-large">
        <div class="shot-media">
          <img
            src={editorShot.src}
            width={editorShot.width}
            height={editorShot.height}
            alt="Editor with design-notes.md open on the remote server"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Edit remote files in place.</strong> UTF-8 up to 2&nbsp;MiB, atomic saves and
          stale-write detection.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="shot-pair">
        <figure class="shot">
          <div class="shot-media">
            <img
              src={paletteShot.src}
              width={paletteShot.width}
              height={paletteShot.height}
              alt="Command palette searching for connections and actions"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong><kbd>⌘K</kbd> opens the command palette.</strong>{" "}
            <kbd>⌘1</kbd> and <kbd>⌘2</kbd> switch panes; <kbd>⌘J</kbd> opens the queue.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="shot">
          <div class="shot-media">
            <img
              src={permissionsShot.src}
              width={permissionsShot.width}
              height={permissionsShot.height}
              alt="Permissions dialog with an octal mode and read, write and execute checkboxes"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Octal and symbolic modes.</strong> Per-entry errors, right where the change
            happens.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
